  "text": "BentoPDF\nBack to Tools\nBentoPDF›Merge PDF\nMerge PDF\n\nCombine multiple PDFs into one file. Preserves Bookmarks.\n\nClick to select a file or drag and drop\n\nPDFs or Images\n\nYour files never leave your device.\n\nAdd More Files\nClear All\nFile Mode\nPage Mode\n\nHow it works:\n\nClick and drag the  icon to change the order of the files.\nIn the \"Pages\" box for each file, you can specify ranges (e.g., \"1-3, 5\") to merge only those pages.\nLeave the \"Pages\" box blank to include all pages from that file.\nchapter-a.pdf\nPages (e.g., 1-3, 5) - Total: 3\nchapter-b.pdf\nPages (e.g., 1-3, 5) - Total: 2\nKeep original page labels from each file\nOff (default): the merged PDF uses natural page numbering 1–N. On: each file's original page labels are preserved (may produce duplicate labels).\nRemove duplicate fonts\nMerge PDFs\nSuccess\n\nPDFs merged successfully!\n\nOK\nBentoPDF\n\n© 2026 BentoPDF. All rights reserved.\n\nVersion 2.8.10\n\nEnglish",
